[1mBug 1: [38;5;10mread_line[0m didn't emulate C's [38;5;10mfgets[0m buffer limit[22m ([38;5;10mcity_name_500_chars[0m test)[0m[0m
[0m[0m
C's [38;5;10mfgets(input, 256, stdin)[0m reads at most 255 chars and leaves the remainder in the stdin buffer. The Rust [38;5;10mread_line[0m consumed the entire line regardless of length. When a 500-char city name was input, C would read 255 chars, then the next [38;5;10mfgets[0m for the menu would read the leftover chars (producing "Invalid input"). Rust read all 500 chars in one go.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Fix: Rewrote [38;5;10mread_line[0m to read byte-by-byte, stopping at [38;5;10m\n[0m or after 255 bytes, leaving the rest in the buffer — matching [38;5;10mfgets[0m semantics exactly.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mBug 2: Integer overflow on distance parsing[22m ([38;5;10mdistance_overflow[0m test)[0m[0m
[0m[0m
C's [38;5;10msscanf(input, "%d", &distance)[0m silently truncates large numbers (like [38;5;10m9999999999999[0m) to fit in a 32-bit int via wrapping. Rust's [38;5;10mparse::<i32>()[0m returns an error on overflow.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Fix: Parse as [38;5;10mi64[0m first, then cast to [38;5;10mi32[0m with [38;5;10mas i32[0m, which truncates the same way C does.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mBug 3: Empty city name rejected[22m ([38;5;10mempty_city_name[0m test)[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust [38;5;10madd_node[0m had an [38;5;10mif city_name.is_empty()[0m guard that returned an error. The C code only checks [38;5;10m!city_name[0m (null pointer), not empty strings — it happily accepts an empty city name.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Fix: Removed the [38;5;10mis_empty()[0m check.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mBug 4: Null bytes not handled like C strings[22m ([38;5;10mnull_byte_input[0m test)[0m[0m
[0m[0m
C treats [38;5;10m\0[0m as a string terminator, so [38;5;10m"City\0Name"[0m becomes [38;5;10m"City"[0m. Rust strings can contain null bytes, so the full [38;5;10m"City\0Name"[0m was stored and printed.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Fix: Added truncation at the first [38;5;10m\0[0m byte when processing city name input.[0m[0m
